On Fri, Feb 4, 2011 at 1:53 PM, Till Kamppeter <till.kamppeter@gmail.com>wrote:

> Hi,
>
> Due to a conflict with the TCG Hardcopy WG Tutorial during the
> Trusted Computing Group Members Meeting next week,
> we have MOVED our regular OP Monthly call one week later
> to be combined with our first OP Summit planning call on WEDNESDAY,
> February 16.
>
> As the OpenPrinting Workgroup Meeting of March would be one day before the
> second OP Summit preparation call, we combine this meeting with that
> planning call and so also hold it on a Wednesday, March, 2.
>
> The OpenPrinting Meeting of April would theoretically be on the Tuesday
> before the Summit and therefore we cancel it.
>
> On WEDNESDAY 16 we will talk about the following topics:
>
> * OpenPrinting Summit 2011
>   - Suggestions for topics and schedules
>   - Questions & Answers
> * Common Printing Dialog
>  - Roadmap to complete the dialog until middle of 2011
>  - German government organization rejected further funding, they will
>    not give more than originally offered
>  - Funding by additional parties, especially distributions, needed
> * Project ideas for the Google Summer of Code 2011
> * Possible reschedule of the monthly OP telecon to the first Wednesday
>  of the month.
>
>   Till
>
> ----------
